{"id":"effect-30e59965-dd8c-52f9-b494-06f48a997da0","sessionId":"7f64a5a6-4823-1340-5268-020509e6e15d","turnId":"turn-2f20e3d9bcdfdf448d5c0f9ea1a01d36","inputEntryId":"user-turn-2f20e3d9bcdfdf448d5c0f9ea1a01d36-1","createdAt":1794276718623,"updatedAt":1794276718645,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"effect","title":"file_system.read_file","detail":{"toolName":"file_system.read_file","display":{"summary":"Reading ANSWER.md","content":null,"suffix":"","verb":"Reading","message":"ANSWER.md","settledVerb":"Read","settledMessage":"ANSWER.md","statusText":"Reading file"},"kind":"file_read","input":{"filePath":"ANSWER.md","offset":null,"limit":2000}},"state":{"status":"completed","outputText":"","display":{"success":true,"verb":"Read","message":"33 lines from ANSWER.md","warnings":[],"approvalNote":null,"suffix":""},"output":{"filePath":"/private/tmp/h-cB0QtO/ANSWER.md","content":"# Fix for System Prompt Caching with Long-Term Memory\n\n## Problem\nEvery `save_fact` call was causing the next LLM call to pay full price for the entire system prompt (~1000 tokens) instead of reading it from cache. This happened because the system prompt was built as a single concatenated string of `INSTRUCTIONS + athlete_context(a, today)`, and when `save_fact` modified the athlete's facts, the entire system prompt changed, invalidating the cache.\n\n## Solution\nSplit the system prompt into two separate messages in `build_system()`:\n\n1. **Static INSTRUCTIONS** - Passed as a plain text message without `cache_control`. This allows the LLM to cache the static instructions independently across all requests.\n\n2. **Dynamic athlete_context** - Passed as a separate text message with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`. This part changes with each athlete and with each fact update, so it remains ephemeral.\n\n## Change Made\nIn `bot.py`, modified the `build_system()` function:\n\n```python\ndef build_system(a, today):\n    # Split into static instructions (cacheable) and dynamic athlete context (ephemeral).\n    # This prevents memory writes (save_fact) from evicting the static instructions from cache.\n    return [\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": INSTRUCTIONS},\n        {\"type\": \"text\", \"text\": athlete_context(a, today), \"cache_control\": {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}},\n    ]\n```\n\nPreviously, both parts were concatenated into a single string and marked as ephemeral, causing the entire system prompt to be re-cached whenever the athlete context changed.\n\n## Expected Impact\nAfter this change:\n- The static INSTRUCTIONS (~1000 tokens) will be cached once and reused across all messages\n- Only the athlete context (small, ~50-100 tokens) will be re-processed when facts change\n- `save_fact` calls will no longer cause the next message to pay full price for the system prompt\n- Cache hit rate should improve significantly, especially for athletes who frequently add facts in their first week\n","numLines":33,"startLine":1,"requestedOffset":null,"requestedLimit":2000,"totalLines":null,"wasTruncated":false},"decision":"execute","durationMs":0.0,"approvalType":"always","approvalSource":"bypass"}}
