{"id":"assistant-a67c61cd-84f0-5e3d-84b4-a3424049ed0c","sessionId":"7f64a5a6-4823-1340-5268-020509e6e15d","turnId":"turn-2f20e3d9bcdfdf448d5c0f9ea1a01d36","inputEntryId":"user-turn-2f20e3d9bcdfdf448d5c0f9ea1a01d36-1","createdAt":1794276732092,"updatedAt":1794276732092,"generationStatus":"completed","relatedEntryId":null,"type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Perfect! All tests pass. Let me create a final summary of what was done:\n\n## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the caching issue where `save_fact` calls were causing the next LLM call to pay full price for the entire system prompt. Here's what was changed:\n\n### The Problem\nThe original `build_system()` function concatenated the static `INSTRUCTIONS` with the dynamic `athlete_context(a, today)` into a single message, both marked as ephemeral. When `save_fact` modified the athlete's facts, the entire system prompt changed, causing a cache miss and requiring the full ~1000 tokens to be reprocessed.\n\n### The Solution\nModified the `build_system()` function in `bot.py` to split the system prompt into two separate messages:\n1. **Static INSTRUCTIONS** - Passed as a plain text message without `cache_control`, allowing it to be cached independently across all requests\n2. **Dynamic athlete_context** - Passed as a separate text message with `cache_control: {\"type\": \"ephemeral\"}`, which changes with each athlete and each fact update\n\n### Files Changed\n- **bot.py** - Modified the `build_system()` function (lines 128-135)\n- **ANSWER.md** - Created documentation explaining the fix\n\n### Expected Impact\n- The static INSTRUCTIONS (~1000 tokens) will now be cached once and reused across all messages\n- Only the athlete context (~50-100 tokens) will be re-processed when facts change\n- `save_fact` calls will no longer cause the next message to pay full price for the system prompt\n- Cache hit rate should improve significantly, especially for new athletes who frequently add facts\n\nAll tests pass and the fix is backward compatible with the Anthropic Messages API."}],"source":"harness","userDisplayContent":null,"outcome":{"type":"committed"}}
